[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS015
TITLE: Restart a failed local computer without a second clearance authority
STATEMENT: >>>
When a local computer stops and later restarts, it shall rejoin the group by receiving the committed log before it may issue clearances. It shall not issue from a log prefix that the surviving authority has already superseded. Acceptance is a restarted member that matches the survivor occupancy after replay, and that refuses a command while it is still catching up.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Recovery must not create a second authority with a stale history.
<<<
DAL: A
REQUIREMENT_LEVEL: High-Level
VERIFICATION: PropEr
ASSUMPTIONS: Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.
RELATIONS:
